message: "If you use these data or code, please cite the article and this archive."
title: "What explains public support for plastic policy? A comparative study of Nigeria and Ghana: data, code and outputs"
abstract: >-
  De-identified survey data (740 respondents in Nigeria and Ghana), a single Jupyter notebook
  (Python and R) and every table and figure for the article "What explains public support for
  plastic policy? A comparative study of Nigeria and Ghana". The notebook covers measurement
  invariance, multi-group structural equation modelling, latent class analysis, machine learning
  with cross-country transfer and SHAP, and coding of open-ended answers.
